## AIWG SDLC Framework

This project uses [AIWG](https://aiwg.io) for SDLC orchestration with DeepSeek Harness.

### Skills

Kernel skills deploy flat to `.agents/skills/` (natively scanned by DeepSeek
Harness); the bulk framework/addon payload deploys to `.dsh/.aiwg/skills/`
(index-discoverable, not flat-scanned — keeps session catalogs lean). User-scope
deploys land in `~/.agents/skills/`.

```bash
aiwg use sdlc --provider dsh        # redeploy / refresh
aiwg list                           # inventory
```

**Discover-first protocol:** most AIWG skills are not in your context. Run
`aiwg discover "<need>"`, then `aiwg show skill <name>` to load the body.

### Artifacts

SDLC artifacts stored in `.aiwg/`:

```
.aiwg/
├── intake/        # Project intake forms
├── requirements/  # User stories, use cases
├── architecture/  # SAD, ADRs
├── planning/      # Phase plans
├── testing/       # Test strategy, plans
├── security/      # Threat models
└── deployment/    # Deployment plans
```

### Natural Language Workflows

- "Run intake on this idea"
- "Generate a threat model for this design"
- "Create an architecture decision record"
- "What's the project status?"
- "Run security review"

### MCP Server (Optional)

DSH's MCP client plugin can connect to AIWG's server — add to `cordis.yml`:

```yaml
- id: aiwg-mcp
  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client'
  config:
    serverName: aiwg
    transport: stdio
    command: npx
    args: ['aiwg', 'mcp', 'serve']
```

